<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — MorphoEval overall 91.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py` (consensus score 91.4/100, up from 52.7/100 in Pass 1). The remediated script implements L-BFGS-B energy minimization of the unilateral mantle-margin functional along the *Murex pecten* siphonal canal (`solve_murex_siphonal_comb`, L168-281, N=16.0 primary spines + intercalated spinules), solves Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica loop closure from open-gutter frond to sealed hollow tube (`solve_kirchhoff_elastica_spine_loop`, L287-338), synthesizes 3-stage *Chicoreus ramosus* fractal frond serrations (`synthesize_chicoreus_fractal_frond`, L341-385; k_2^*/k_1^* = 3.8011, k_3^*/k_1^* = 8.4258), models episodic triradiate varix whorl accretion (`simulate_episodic_varix_whorls`, L391-443; Delta_phi = 120.0 deg), validates 10 muricid species (r = 1.0000 for k_2/k_1, r = 0.9987 for spine count), and segments n=16 primary comb spines (CV = 0.2092) on the SHA-256-locked *Murex pecten* specimen, backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.4/100 (faithfulness 91.1, reproducibility 92.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py at HEAD, image/png, 923113 B, 2640×1680 px, artifact_sha256 16175ede1e6af03115c6122eba4c4df9db284bf4ccefc8814fe1c1ad92afa20b (sha256 16175ede1e6af03115c6122eba4c4df9db284bf4ccefc8814fe1c1ad92afa20b), spec_fingerprint 2b94e7a03cd347db53de50ca64fa7292e03536c1d004ec54908d722b5d7edd8a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2b94e7a03cd347db53de50ca64fa7292e03536c1d004ec54908d722b5d7edd8a; artifact_sha256: 16175ede1e6af03115c6122eba4c4df9db284bf4ccefc8814fe1c1ad92afa20b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json=c73e5d2ac5c13cd5..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/murex_pecten_aperture_specimen.jpg=2f87d4ec30ebec6a..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/paper_citations.bib=fc39398ba54f69e1..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/scout_manifest.json=53cb565add07b28d...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the planar Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica loop solver to a 3D finite-strain Koiter shell finite-element model (Rudraraju et al. 2019 PLoS Comput. Biol.) to resolve oblique spiral cord intersections with varix spines.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate micro-CT cross-sectional measurements of mantle edge thickness gradients h(s) across ontogenetic instars in Chicoreus ramosus." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.14e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Parameter expressivity: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Spans subcritical smooth shell (gamma=0.96), open-gutter frond (gamma=1.26), kissing self-contact threshold (gamma=1.42), and sealed tubular *Murex* spine (gamma=1.68), resolves 3 hierarchical frond generations (h1=0.42, h2=0.0708, h3=0.0245 mm), evaluates 10 muricid species across 5 subclades, and exposes `--E`, `--K-s`, `--gamma-varix`, `--seed`, `--skip-gif`, `--self-test`, and `--verify-only` CLI flags (L885-922)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
